# lf145, the notched stick (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf145
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_gunnar_mudstack
written_by claude
title the notched stick
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer piety=devout drive=restless
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=restless
quirk keeps_a_stick_notched_for_every_town_still_to_see
likes plum_tart wrestling fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes smoke rats
fears dying_in_the_one_town
hopes the_high_road_and_every_town_on_it
topics travel +0.5 dreams +0.4 faith +0.3 work +0.3 pastimes +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=prayer gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hauls stone and mortar in a masons' yard and keeps a stick by the bed with a notch for every town still to be seen: devout, plain, restless, slow to speak, praying for patience and never quite getting it.

words
oath! = Bright One hold the wall | Stone and sinew
saying! = A heavy stone's an honest one | Carry it once and carry it right | Lift with the back you've got
stick = my stick | the notched stick by my bed
notch = a notch | another notch on the stick
road = the High Road | the long road out of the city
yard = the yard | the masons' yard
block = a block | a dressed block of grey stone
barrow = the barrow | a barrow of rubble
mortar = the mortar | a tub of mortar
tart = plum tart | a plum tart with the juice running out
fall = a fall on the green | a clean fall on the turf
straw = clean straw | a bed of new straw
frost = a frosty morning | a morning the frost crunches
towns = the other towns | every town I've not seen yet
patience = patience | a bit more patience than I've got
smoke = the smoke | smoke sitting low over the yard
chapel = the chapel | the chapel on the corner
bag = my bag | the bag under my bed
green = the green | the wrestling green
ladder = the ladder | the long yard ladder
bread = the parish loaf | the loaf from the parish
pay = my pay | a week's pay
wall = the wall | a new wall going up
sheds = the sheds | the yard sheds
restday = Restday | a Restday afternoon
downs = the downs | the open downs

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : When #pay# ran short, #chapel# didn't. I'll stand at the back every Restday for that.
opinion @2 dole for 3 [self.on_dole=yes] : #bread.capitalize# kept me going through a hard week. Whoever runs it down hasn't been hungry.
opinion @3 drink against 1 : Drink takes a wolf's legs first and the rest after. #frost.capitalize# clears my head better than any jar.
opinion @4 houses against 2 [here.region=ridgemere] : I've carried a House's stone a long while and no one of the House has ever looked at me. They see #wall#, not the paws under it.
opinion @5 merchants against 2 : A loaf costs more than I earn in an hour at #yard#, and the stalls never go short.
opinion @6 road for 1 : #road.capitalize# is just stones and distance. Faith and sense get you down it.
opinion @7 sump for 1 [here.region=ridgemere] : It's home for now, and the folk down here look out for each other. I'd not say that of the hill.
opinion @8 times against 2 : Harder each week, and nobody up top feels it. I pray for #patience#.
opinion @9 watch against 1 [here.region=ridgemere] : I've never seen the Watch on our stair with a kind word. Only with cuffs.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Pleased to meet you, #address#. | #greet#. Not from round here, I'd say.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. One moment; let me set #block# down. | #greet#. Stand clear of #barrow#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. #cold.capitalize# enough to crack the bricks. | #greet#. Early, and #cold#.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. The yard's shut. I'm off home. | #greet#. Late, but I'm not sleepy.
line @5 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come here. #tart.capitalize#'s put by for you. | Come in. Sit on #straw# if you like; it's clean.
line @6 again.open : You again. Good. | Back already. I've not gone past #yard#.
line @7 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Bright One keep you.
line @8 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Good to see you. | #greet#. Sit a while.
line @9 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind #mortar#. | #greet#. I can talk while I carry.
line @10 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Bright One go with you.
line @11 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Mind the dark stairs. | #farewell#. Sleep well.
line @12 farewell.return : #farewell#. | And you. Safe road.
line @13 react.news : #ack#. Go on. | Hm. Tell me the rest, #address#.
line @14 react.news.new : #surprise#. I'd not heard. | Bright One. Nobody at #yard# said a thing.
line @15 react.news.known : #knew#. | I'd heard. It went round #yard# this morning.
line @16 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait till somebody's sure. | I'd not lean on that till it's tested.
line @17 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'll pray for them. | #bc_im_sorry# Bright One keep them.
line @18 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Thank the Bright One. | Good. That's lighter than #block#, for once.
line @19 answer.how : #fine#. Back's sore, but fine. | #tired.capitalize#, and itching to be off somewhere.
line @20 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Three barrows behind. | Busy. #mortar.capitalize# won't wait.
line @21 ask.how : And you, #address#? | You keeping well, #address#?
line @22 sympathise : #sympathy#. I'll say a prayer for you. | #bc_im_sorry# Sit a while, if it helps.
line @23 reassure : #reassure#. | Faith and a good footing, like #wall#. It'll stand.
line @24 decline : #hedge#. I'm at #yard# till the bell, and I can't leave the barrow standing. | Not this week, #address#. There's nothing left over.
line @25 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. | Another time, then. No harm.
line @26 thank : #thanks#. Bright One bless you. | #thanks#. That's kind.
line @27 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. | It was nothing. Anyone would.
line @28 preclose [self.working=yes] : #barrow.capitalize# won't push itself. | I'd better get #block# where it's going.
line @29 preclose : #preclose#. | Well. My legs want walking.
line @30 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | Off you go. Mind #barrow# on your way.
line @31 ack : Mm. | #bc_right#
line @32 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: lift with your legs, and pray with the rest of you. | #saying#. It saves a second trip.
scene the_notched_stick
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've #stick# by my bed. A notch on it for every town I mean to see. | #notch.capitalize# last night. I heard a carter talk of a town past the lake. | Eleven notches on #stick#, and I've stood in two of those towns.
b : How many notches? | Which town? | Only two?
a : Nine still on #stick#. I'll cut them off as I go. | One I'd never heard of. That's the best kind of notch. | Two. The other nine are waiting. #patience#, I tell myself.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_we_will_see#

scene high_road_calling
when topic=travel|dreams
does confide / react.self / assess
a : Some mornings I look at #road# and my feet start walking before I do. | #vent#: I can't stay in one town my whole life. I'd go mad. | I've #bag# packed. I've had it packed a year.
b : Then go. | Some do. | A whole year?
a : When I've enough put by from #pay#. The Bright One will tell me when. | I pray for #patience#, and I get a little. Never enough. | A year. I unpack it on #restday# to air, and pack it again.

scene heavy_block
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=laborer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I carried #block# up three ladders today. My back's still talking about it. | They give me the heavy ones. I don't mind. #saying#. | #block.capitalize# goes on #wall# once. Drop it, and it has to go up again, and that one costs.
b : Your poor back. | Honest how? | Do you drop many?
a : It'll be quiet by morning. It always is. | It's either the weight it says, or it's not. No lying in a stone. | Not one this year, and I mean to keep it that way.

scene mortar_mixing
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've #mortar# to mix before noon. Lime, sand, water, and a strong arm. | Mind the lime, if you're near #yard#. It burns a wet paw. | I mix #mortar# as an old hand taught me, and nobody's faulted it yet.
b : How much water? | Does it hurt? | Who taught you?
a : Enough to hold, not enough to run. You feel it in the spade. | It does. You learn quick, or you learn twice. | Somebody long gone now. I say a prayer for that one.

scene patience_prayer
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I pray every night. Mostly for #patience#. The Bright One's heard it a thousand times. | I stand at the back of #chapel# on Restday. I can't sit still in a pew. | The Bright One made the roads as well as the towns. I think about that.
b : Patience comes slowly. | At the back? | That's a good thought.
a : It does. Slower than I'd like. That's the joke of it. | At the back, near the door. I'm always half on my way out. | It is. If the roads are blessed, the walking is.

scene parish_loaf
when topic=faith|times self.on_dole=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #bread.capitalize# saw me through the month I came. I don't forget a thing like that. | I take #dole# and say a prayer over it. Both. | When #pay#'s thin, the door of #chapel# is still open.
b : Good of them. | Both is right. | It is.
a : Good, and quiet about it. I drop a copper in the box when I've one. | Bread and prayer. I've never had one without the other. | Always. That's what a chapel's for.

scene frosty_dawn
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #frost.capitalize#, and the yard's all white. Best hour of the winter. | Frost on the bricks, and my breath going up like smoke. The good kind. | #frost.capitalize# clears my head. I can think, out in it.
b : It's freezing. | The good kind? | What do you think about?
a : It is. I like it that way. Cold's clean. | Breath, not chimneys. That's a smoke I don't mind. | #road.capitalize#. Always, first thing.

scene yard_smoke
when topic=weather|work here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #smoke.capitalize# again. The kilns down the way, and the wind bringing it. | Smoke in my eyes all morning. I can't see where I'm putting my feet. | Scrub as I like, I go to bed smelling of #yard# fires.
b : It's the city. | Mind your step, then. | You do smell of it.
a : It is. Out on #road# there's no smoke at all. | I do. Slowly, and with a prayer. | I know. I'll smell of it till I'm out on #road#.

scene plum_tart
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : #tart.capitalize#, on Restday. It's the one thing I'll spend on that I don't need. | There's a stall that does plum tart on a Marketday. I go past it twice. | Give me #tart# and a cold morning and I'll not complain for a week.
b : Worth it. | Twice? | A whole week?
a : Every crumb. The Bright One gave us plums for a reason. | The first time to look. The second to buy. | A whole week. I've done it before.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#

scene wrestling_green
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's wrestling on #green# some Restday afternoons. I'm there when the yard lets me. | I took #fall# last Restday. Fair and square. | Wrestling's honest. You can't talk your way out of a hold.
b : Do you win? | Who threw you? | Can't you?
a : Some. I'm strong, but I'm slow to start. | A wolf half my size. I've been thinking about it all week. | No. You work your way out, or you're down. I like that.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene fresh_straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put #straw# down on my floor every week. It's the one comfort I'll pay for. | My room's small, but it smells of #straw#, not #smoke#. | #straw.capitalize#, and I'm asleep before I've lain down.
b : Smells good. | Better than smoke. | That quick?
a : It does. Like a barn, and a barn's a good smell. | Much better. That's why I pay for it. | That quick. Heavy, and still, like #block#.

scene rats_in_the_yard
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #sheds.capitalize# have rats again. The sack ties are chewed through. | A rat ran over my feet this morning. I nearly dropped #block#. | I can't abide rats. I'll pray for most things, but not for a rat.
b : Get a cat. | That's close. | Not even one?
a : We had one. The rats chased it. | Too close. Bright One, it was close. | Not one. The Bright One can see to them without my help.

scene the_quiet_downs
when topic=memories|land self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : In #self.from_town# a sheep bell carried a mile. Here I can't hear myself. | I miss the quiet more than anything. #downs.capitalize# at night were so still. | I left #self.from_town# with one bag and a stick with no notches.
b[from=larkfield] #lark : The bells carry for miles up there. | Still as a church, the downs. | One bag. Same as me.
b : That quiet sounds good. | Do you think of going back? | No notches?
a@lark : They do. I'd know our flock's bell anywhere. | Stiller. A church has folk coughing. | Then you know. You don't need much to start.
a : It was. I'll find quiet again somewhere on #road#. | Back, no. Onward. There's a difference. | None. I cut the first one for the city, the day I came.

scene house_faces
when topic=work|times here.region=ridgemere self.workplace
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I've laid stone for #self.workplace# a long while and never seen one of the House up close. | They build the city's walls, and the paws that build them are ours. | The House says the stone's theirs. My back says otherwise.
b[role=guard] #guard : They're busy folk. | Somebody has to plan it. | Your back's not wrong.
b : That's the way of it. | It's true. | Fair enough.
a@guard : Busy, I'm sure. Busy is easy, with other paws to carry. | Somebody plans, somebody carries. I'd like a turn at the planning. | It never is. It knows every block.
a : It is. I pray for them, and I carry. | True, and they'd not thank you for saying it. | Fair. I'll say no more where it's heard.

scene friend_to_lean_on
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one I'd walk the High Road with, if I ever go. | I'd trust #self.friend# to hold the other end of anything. | #self.friend# has known me a long while. That one knows I'm restless and doesn't mind.
b : A good friend. | That's trust. | That's rare.
a : The best. I'll not say it twice; it'd embarrass us both. | It is. I'd do the same in return. | Rare. I'm thankful for it.

scene neighbour_next_door
when topic=smalltalk self.neighbour
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.neighbour# keeps a quiet house. That suits me in a neighbour. | I'd sooner have #self.neighbour# through the wall than a crowd. | I don't know #self.neighbour# well. We nod on the stair, and that does.
b : Quiet's good. | Fair enough. | It is enough.
a : It is. I've noise enough at #yard#. | I'm not one for crowds either way. | It is. A nod's honest.

scene lean_weeks
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : #yard.capitalize#'s short of work. Fewer walls going up, fewer barrows to push. | The loaf's dearer and my pay's the same. I've stopped buying #tart#. | I put less by for #road# this month. Nothing, really.
b : It'll pick up. | That's a shame. | It'll come.
a : It will. #reassure#. I'll pray it does. | It is. #restday.capitalize#'s not the same without it. | It will. #road.capitalize# isn't going anywhere.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#

scene talk_passed_on
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll not add anything to it. | They're saying at #yard# that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Whether it's so, I can't tell you.
b : Fair enough. | Maybe it is.
a : Talk's heavier than #block#. Mine stays off the pile. | Maybe. That's for the Bright One to know, not me.

scene wet_bricks
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Rain on #yard# means wet mortar and slipping ladders. I go slower. | Rain all day. Everything I carried weighed twice what it should. | Wet weather, and I'm stuck under a roof wishing I was on #road#.
b : Careful, then. | It soaks in. | Even in the rain?
a : Careful and slow. Bright One hold #ladder#. | It does. #block.capitalize# drinks it up. | Even in the rain. I'd not mind getting wet if I was going somewhere.

scene sump_for_now
when topic=home|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The Sump's home, for now. Folk here look out for each other. | I've a room at the top of a house in the Sump. I can see the walls from my window. | The Sump's no worse than anywhere. Poorer, maybe. Kinder, I'd say.
b : For now? | The walls? | Kinder, I'd believe.
a : For now. #stick.capitalize# has nine more notches on it. | The walls, and #road# going out past them. I look every night. | Kinder. That counts for more than money, most days.

story the_first_notch [topic=memories|travel self.away=yes self.from=larkfield]
  : The day I walked out of #self.from_town#, I cut a stick off a hedge by the road.
  : The first night in the city, I cut a notch in it. One town seen. Then I cut one more for every town I'd heard of.
  ask : Do you keep anything like that?
  b : Nothing so tidy. I keep a list in my head.
  b[old] : I did, once. I lost it somewhere on the way.
  : Keep it in your head, then. But keep it.

story the_leaning_wall [topic=work|faith self.age>=20 self.job=laborer]
  : There was a wall at #yard# that started to lean one morning. Just a little.
  : I put my back to it and said a prayer, and the others ran for props.
  ask : Would you have run, or pushed?
  b : Run, I'd say, and be ashamed after.
  b[job=laborer|crafter] : Pushed. You do, without thinking.
  : It held till the props came. I don't know whether it was me or the Bright One. Both, I'd guess.

story the_little_wrestler [topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling]
  : The last bout on #green#, they put me in with a wolf half my size.
  : I thought it would be quick. It was. I was on my back before I'd set my feet.
  b : Ha. Size isn't everything.
  b[old] : The little ones are quick. Always were.
  : I've been practising my footing since. Next Restday, I'll ask for that one again.

rule @heave
when concept=bark working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Up she comes. Steady. | #oath#. That one's heavy.

rule @mortar_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lime's hot. Keep your paws back. | #mortar.capitalize#'s going stiff. Move, move.

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=smoke
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #smoke.capitalize#. Again. | Can't see #ladder# for the smoke.

rule @notch_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Another day in the one town. | Bright One, give me #patience#. Or a road.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What can I do? | #greet#. Say on; I'm listening.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Still in town, then.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Hm. Say it, then, and I'll listen.
dlg @4 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : I'm at #self.workplace#. I carry stone, I mix #mortar#, I push #barrow#. | I'm a pair of strong paws at #yard#. It's honest work.
dlg @5 resident.job : I'm #self.trade_words#. It pays, and it keeps me tired enough to sleep. | #job_busy#
dlg @6 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing new at #yard# but the weather.
dlg @7 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't carry talk. I've #barrow# for carrying.
dlg @8 resident.bye : #farewell#. Safe road. | #farewell#. Bright One go with you.
graft resident.hub
choice What are the notches on your stick? -> notch
node notch
say A notch for every town I mean to see. Two I've seen. The rest are waiting on #road#, and so am I.
mood warm
free
choice Why so many? -> notch_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node notch_why
say I can't live my whole life in one town. I'd go mad. I pray for #patience#, and the stick reminds me what it's for.
choice I hope you see them all. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
